{ ================================================================================
  S3_S - VOLATILITY SQUEEZE SHORT STRATEGY
  Signal Name : S3_VolSqueezeShort
  MC Load Name: STRATEGY_GEN_S3_VolSqueezeShort
  Version     : v1.9.6-OPT-PROD  (2026-07-06 PROMOTED to live_simulation, replaces v1.8.0-PROD)
                Base: v1.9.6-ANTIHUNT (Config B + 5-param OPT)
                Architecture: Data1=1M, Data2=60M, Data3=Daily

  PROMOTE 2026-07-06:
    - Rule #18 quantitative gates: 7/7 PASS (MC/Bootstrap/Sensitivity/Stress + concentration)
    - WFA: Path A exemption granted (low-freq short structural)
    - Portfolio Correlation with S3_L: EXEMPT (strategies are NOT mirror per user ruling)
    - Backtest (Config B + OPT, xlsx 2026-07-06):
        71 trades / Net +731K / PF 1.749 / MDD -17.17% / Sharpe +0.549 / WR 49.3%
    - MC 10K: 95% MDD -20.47% (v1.9.5 was -30.64% FAIL boundary)
    - Bootstrap 10K: P(Net>0)=95%, P(PF>1)=95%
    - Stress Test 6/6 Event-Net PASS (E2 2022 bear +153K, E5 Trump +190K, E6 06-cluster +343K)
    - Anti-Hunt L1+L2 default OFF (BWRank guard default ON as bug fix)
    - 5-param GA OPT: BWPctile 40, StopATRMult 3.25, SP_Trigger 2.0, Hunt_Max_Stops 4, ML_Score 35
    - v1.8.0-PROD archived to strategies/research/archive/S3_S_v180_replaced_20260706/

  v1.9.6 NEW FEATURES (Round 1, 7 items, user 2026-07-04 ruling):
    Motivation: Night-session stop hunting observed starting 2026-06.
    Hunt pattern: opponents spike price to trigger stops in thin liquidity,
    then price reverts. S3_S BB breakout is a classic stop-cluster zone.

    ITEM 1 - Night SL Widening (Anti-Hunt L1, default OFF)
      NightSL_Widen_On + NightSL_Mult 1.3 + time gates 22:00-05:00
      Frozen SL distance x Mult during night to survive spike hunt.
    ITEM 2 - Confirmation SL (Anti-Hunt L2, default OFF)
      ConfirmSL_On + ConfirmSL_Bars 2. SL fires only when N consecutive
      1M K close beyond SL level. Filters single-K spike hunt.
    ITEM 3 - BWRank Equal-BW Guard (Bug fix, default ON)
      When all lookback BW = current, v_BWCount = 0 -> BWRank = 0 ->
      v_Squeeze = True (false positive). Guard forces False when count = 0.
    ITEM 4 - Mid Exit Confirmation Bars (default 1 = v1.9.5 behavior)
      Optional 2 consecutive Close > MidBand for safer mid-band exit.
    ITEM 5 - Mid Exit Peak Min ATR (default 0 = v1.9.5 behavior)
      Suppress Mid Exit unless Peak_Profit >= v_ATR x MidExit_PeakMinATR.
    ITEM 6 - SP Peak Min Pts (default 0 = v1.9.5 behavior)
      P0.5 SP Priority Fire requires Peak_Profit_Pts >= SP_Peak_Min_Pts.
    ITEM 7 - SP Night Volume Confirm (default OFF)
      Night P0.5 fire also requires Volume > Avg(Volume, N).

  BACK-COMPAT: All new features default to v1.9.5 behavior except
               BWRank guard (bug fix, default ON).
               Full baseline reproduction: set all v1.9.6 gates OFF/0.

  v1.9.5 BACKTEST EVIDENCE (2026-07-03 GA-best):
    68 trades / Net +513.4K / PF 1.574 / MDD -19.05% / WR 50%
    Rule #18: 3/5 pass (MC/Bootstrap PASS, MDD boundary FAIL by 0.64%)

  v1.9.4 BACKTEST EVIDENCE (2026-07-02):
    73 trades / Net -23.8K / PF 0.97 / MDD -29.7pct. Two residual flaws:
    FLAW 1 (marginal thrust): T73 broke prior hunt low by only 1 point
      (42344 vs 42343), entered, V-reversed -> -93.8K largest single loss.
      Fresh-thrust gate lacks a minimum-force requirement.
    FLAW 2 (churn episodes): 9 of 17 hunt episodes were slow-grind /
      bottoming phases where each marginal new low triggered an entry,
      shallow bounce triggered 1M_Exit, repeated. 9 churn episodes
      -369.6K vs 8 clean-trend episodes +345.8K = net -23.8K.
    POSITIVE: 2026-06-06 main crash PERFECTLY captured (T70-72 staircase
      +279.8K). Bounce re-entry clusters eliminated. 1M_Exit functional.

  v1.9.5 SOLUTION (two independent quality gates):
    GATE A - Thrust Margin (blocks marginal breaks like T73):
      Entry requires Close of Data2 < v_Hunt_Low - Thrust_Margin_ATR * ATR
      Default 0.25 x ATR (~37-50 pts). A 1-point break cannot qualify.
      GA range: 0 to 0.5 (0 = disabled, reverts to v1.9.4 behavior).
    GATE B - Hunt Circuit Breaker (kills churn episodes):
      v_Hunt_StopCount tracks consecutive 1M_Exit stop-outs per episode.
      After Hunt_Max_Stops (default 3) consecutive 1M_Exit losses,
      the hunt is force-DISARMed. Any non-1M exit (TP/SP/Mid) resets
      the counter to 0 (episode is proving profitable).
      Counter resets on ARM (new episode) but NOT on repeated squeeze
      bars within the same episode.
      GA range: 2 to 5 (3 verified: 2 would kill T72 +128K).
    INTERACTION MATRIX:
      Marginal thrust + fresh episode    -> BLOCKED by Gate A
      Marginal thrust + exhausted episode -> BLOCKED by Gate A + B
      Real thrust + fresh episode         -> ENTER (desired behavior)
      Real thrust + exhausted episode     -> BLOCKED by Gate B
  Symbol      : TXF1 (Taiwan Stock Index Futures Front Month)
  Platform    : MultiCharts 12 PowerLanguage x64
  Timeframe   : Data1 = 1M (execution) + Data2 = 60M (decision/indicators) + Data3 = Daily (regime)
  Class       : Volatility Regime (C class) - Short only (Rule R-6 split)
  Direction   : Short only

  CHART SETUP REQUIRED:
    Data1 = TXF1 1M
    Data2 = TXF1 60M
    Data3 = TXF1 Daily
    MaxBarsBack >= 1000 (covers Daily MA50 via Data3)
    IntrabarOrderGeneration = FALSE

  CHANGELOG:
    v1.9.5 (2026-07-02): Thrust margin + hunt circuit breaker
         Gate A (marginal thrust filter):
            - NEW input Thrust_Margin_ATR (0.25): entry requires break
              below v_Hunt_Low by at least Thrust_Margin_ATR * ATR
            - Blocks 1-point marginal breaks (T73: -93.8K would be blocked)
            - GA range 0-0.5 (0 disables, reverts to v1.9.4 behavior)
         Gate B (hunt circuit breaker):
            - NEW input Hunt_Max_Stops (3): max consecutive 1M_Exit
              stop-outs per hunt episode before forced DISARM
            - NEW var v_Hunt_StopCount: incremented on 1M_Exit, reset
              on non-1M exit (profitable trade breaks the streak)
            - NEW var v_Was_1M_Stop: flag bridges the fill-bar gap
              (v_1M_ExitFired is cleared in Section 9.5 before
              Section 12 can read it; this flag persists)
            - ARM (new episode) resets counter; repeated squeeze bars
              within same episode do NOT reset
            - GA range 2-5 (3 verified: 2 would kill T72 +128K)

    v1.9.4 (2026-07-02): Hunt state machine (priority-ordered per user ruling)
         P1 (Q2 fix - no re-entry into bounce):
            - Fresh-thrust gate: entry requires Close of Data2 < v_Hunt_Low
              (below EVERY low the hunt episode has printed so far)
            - After a stop-out the bounce closes sit above the crash low
              -> blocked; only a NEW sell-off taking out the low re-enters
            - Date cooldown superseded: Use_Cooldown (False) new input;
              same-day re-entry on a fresh thrust is now allowed
              (v1.9.0 evidence: the profitable 06-05 leg came AFTER the
              morning bounce, same date)
         P2 (Q4 fix - window must never expire):
            - REMOVED SqzMemory bar-count window entirely
            - Hunt stays armed while structure is broken (close < MidBand)
            - Disarm only on structure repair: v_Squeeze=False AND
              Close of Data2 > v_MidBand; re-arm on next squeeze
         - REMOVED: SqzMemory input, v_SqueezeBar / v_RecentSqueeze vars
         - NEW: Use_Cooldown input, v_Hunt_Active / v_Hunt_Low vars,
              Section 10.5 hunt-low updater (runs AFTER entry check)
         - All v1.9.2 exit-side logic UNCHANGED

    v1.9.3 (2026-07-02): Squeeze memory entry window
         - NEW input SqzMemory (12): entry allowed within N 60M bars
           after the last v_Squeeze=True reading (GA range 3-30)
         - NEW vars v_SqueezeBar / v_RecentSqueeze (Section 2 + 6)
         - Entry gate (Section 10): v_Squeeze replaced by v_RecentSqueeze
         - v_SqueezeBar > 0 guard prevents warm-up false positives
         - All v1.9.2 exit-side logic UNCHANGED (isolated verification of
           entry-side fix on top of exit-side fix)
         - NOTE: BB family (BBLen/BBStd/BWLookback/BWPctile) + SqzMemory
           require GA re-optimization: existing values were tuned under
           the inverted count(>) BWRank semantics of v1.8.0

    v1.9.2 (2026-07-01): SP Priority Fire + Tiered Retain
         - Section 1: Added 3 new inputs
             SP_Retain_Tier1_Pct (default 80)
             SP_Retain_Tier2_Pct (default 85)
             SP_Retain_Tier3_Pct (default 90)
             Thresholds hardcoded at 100/200/300 pts
         - Section 2: Added v_SP_Retain_Dynamic variable
         - Section 11:
             a. Layer 2 SP tracking uses v_SP_Retain_Dynamic (tiered)
             b. NEW P0.5 SP Armed Priority Fire block (Market order)
                Fires before S-0 1M_Exit when SP armed and Close >= Floor
             c. S-4 SP Stop retained as backup (only fires if P0.5 misses)
             d. Label naming: SX_VS_SP_Armed (P0.5) vs SX_VS_SP (S-4 backup)
         - All entry logic, factor scoring, other exits: UNCHANGED
         - Parameter values (BB/ATR/Regime/ML_*): UNCHANGED from v1.9.1

    v1.9.1 (2026-07-01): BWRank comparison direction fix
    v1.9.0 (2026-07-01): Data1=1M architecture rewrite
    v1.8.0 (2026-06-29): [see v1.8.0-PROD header for full history]

  ALPHA THESIS: [unchanged from v1.8.0]
  PARAMETERIZATION: [tiered SP retain new; others unchanged]
  CONSTITUTION COMPLIANCE: [unchanged]
  LABEL CONVENTIONS: [unchanged + SX_VS_SP_Armed added]

  STATUS: v1.9.5 EXPERIMENTAL - thrust margin + hunt circuit breaker.
          Acceptance:
          1. T73-type marginal entries (1-point break) MUST be blocked
          2. Churn episodes must self-terminate after 3 consecutive stops
          3. 2026-06-06 main crash T70-72 staircase MUST survive
          4. v1.9.4 clean-trend wins (+345.8K across 8 episodes) preserved
          5. 1M_Exit protection intact (losses capped per trade)
================================================================================ }

